    "blurb": "The Seattle concert delivers a soaring The Other One, an inspired Stella Blue solo, and a flawless Truckin' → Drums → The Other One → Comes A Time sequence. Jerry’s guitar tone shines throughout while Phil’s bass drives the improvisations. An excellent soundboard capture makes this a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
    "review": "July 21, 1972 at the Paramount Northwest Theater finds the Dead locked in a high‑octane groove that rolls from a solid first set into a second‑set marathon of inspired jams. The band builds momentum with a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue before Jerry’s plaintive guitar on Stella Blue lifts the mood, only to explode later into an unforgettable The Other One where his daring interplay with Phil and Bill creates a swirling tapestry of sound. The highlight reel continues with Truckin' soaring into a tight drum break that segues flawlessly into The Other One and resolves beautifully in Comes A Time, all underpinned by Keith’s tasteful keyboard textures and Donna’s backing vocals. The excellent soundboard source captures every nuance – from the crisp snare crack to the warm organ fills – making this performance one of the most rewarding recordings of the 1972 spring tour.",
